/**
 * Compatibility type check against the **0.1.7-rc.2** harness declarations.
 *
 * The DSH STORE's authoritative window currently resolves to the 0.1.7 line
 * (`0.1.7-alpha.2` / `0.1.7-rc.1` / `0.1.7-rc.2`), while the declared peer range
 * `^0.1.5-rc.2 || ^0.2.0-rc.2` intersects none of them — so this gate exists to
 * turn "does 0.1.7 work" into a reading before anything is declared compatible
 * (PL-EN-NW-08; the declaration itself is PL-DI-NW-02's, and the runtime half is
 * PL-TS-IV-07).
 *
 * **Why this file needs a `paths` block at all.** `tsconfig.compat-0.2.0.json` is
 * just an `extends`: the repository's own `node_modules` already *is* 0.2.0-rc.2.
 * The 0.1.7 line cannot be the tree the ordinary check runs on, so
 * `tools/compat-install.mjs` installs it privately under the gitignored
 * `_scratch/` and the four harness specifiers are redirected there. Relative
 * paths only: an absolute one would leak a machine path into the public face, and
 * `npm run check`'s leak guard greps `tsconfig*.json` for exactly that.
 *
 * All four are redirected, not just the two that follow the DSH version line.
 * `cordis` / `schemastery` are the same versions on both lines (IS-062), but
 * leaving them to resolve out of the repository would put two copies of those
 * declaration graphs in one program, which is the shape that produces spurious
 * nominal-type errors.
 *
 * **What a green run means, and does not.** It says `src/**` type-checks against
 * the pinned 0.1.7-rc.2 declaration set — the same coupling `src/pins.ts` asserts
 * against 0.2.0-rc.2, including `_ReasonsCovered` refusing a new turn-end kind.
 * It is not a runtime verification, it does not cover harness packages that are
 * neither pinned nor reachable from the pinned ones, and it covers **one**
 * version: `0.1.7-alpha.2` / `0.1.7-rc.1` are inside the STORE window and outside
 * this gate.
 *
 * ⚠️ **Falsifying this gate needs a mapping that resolves to the wrong file.**
 * Pointing `paths` at a *missing* path does NOT go red: TypeScript falls back to
 * ordinary `node_modules` resolution, silently reads the repository's own 0.2.0
 * tree, and still exits 0. Map a real-but-wrong `.d.ts` instead (IS-072).
 *
 * Run `npm run compat:0.1.7`; deliberately **not** part of `npm run check` (it
 * needs the network and the gitignored `_scratch/`).
 */
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.types.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "paths": {
      "@deepseek-ai/cordis": ["./_scratch/compat-0.1.7-rc.2/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/cordis/lib/types/index.d.ts"],
      "@deepseek-ai/schemastery": ["./_scratch/compat-0.1.7-rc.2/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/schemastery/lib/types/index.d.ts"],
      "@deepseek-ai/dsh-session": ["./_scratch/compat-0.1.7-rc.2/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-session/lib/types/index.d.ts"],
      "@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent": ["./_scratch/compat-0.1.7-rc.2/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent/lib/types/index.d.ts"]
    }
  }
}
